WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:04.370
After months of radio silence, Solo has finally
burst onto the scene.

00:00:04.370 --> 00:00:08.610
The new Star Wars story is the first of Disney's
spinoff films set to explore the life of an

00:00:08.610 --> 00:00:12.919
original trilogy character — in this case
the smuggler Han Solo, played for the first

00:00:12.919 --> 00:00:14.579
time by Alden Ehrenreich.

00:00:14.579 --> 00:00:18.650
Between the Super Bowl teaser and the first
trailer, there's a lot to digest.

00:00:18.650 --> 00:00:20.950
Here are a few details you might have missed.

00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:22.089
New duds

00:00:22.089 --> 00:00:26.369
Han Solo having more or less the same costume
in the original three Star Wars movies and

00:00:26.369 --> 00:00:30.669
The Force Awakens made many fans assume they
would be seeing young Solo sporting the exact

00:00:30.669 --> 00:00:32.480
same look in his standalone film.

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:36.980
But that's not the case: in the Solo trailer,
the young pilot is instead sporting a wide

00:00:36.980 --> 00:00:39.730
variety of interstellar fashions.

00:00:39.730 --> 00:00:40.750
New ships

00:00:40.750 --> 00:00:44.140
The end of the trailer provides one of the
most striking images yet from the new Star

00:00:44.140 --> 00:00:49.180
Wars movies: a Star Destroyer in a dense nebula
dispatching some TIE Fighters in pursuit of

00:00:49.180 --> 00:00:50.660
the Millennium Falcon.

00:00:50.660 --> 00:00:53.579
While we don't know the names of these new
ship models yet, you can see that there's

00:00:53.579 --> 00:00:59.040
an extra laser-shooting pod to the side of
the cockpit, presumably for extra firepower.

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:00.269
New locale

00:01:00.269 --> 00:01:05.000
While the trailer doesn't identify exactly
where in the galaxy this chase is taking place,

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:09.180
speculation is already swirling that the pursuit
may be set near the cloudy area of Kessel,

00:01:09.180 --> 00:01:13.290
which, according the Extended Universe, is
surrounded by a cluster of black holes.

00:01:13.290 --> 00:01:17.080
It stands to reason that those opaque gases
would be dangerous to navigate and would make

00:01:17.080 --> 00:01:21.330
any ship passing through it hard to detect
— key attributes for, say, a smuggler's

00:01:21.330 --> 00:01:22.330
route.

00:01:22.330 --> 00:01:25.550
That's why many fans are speculating that
this footage could be of the famous Kessel

00:01:25.550 --> 00:01:32.110
Run, which Solo made in just 12 parsecs, not
14, as Rey claims in The Force Awakens.

00:01:32.110 --> 00:01:33.290
New droid

00:01:33.290 --> 00:01:37.160
If you've been combing through these clips
looking for actress Phoebe Waller-Bridge,

00:01:37.160 --> 00:01:38.300
look no further.

00:01:38.300 --> 00:01:43.300
She plays this charming droid, L3-37, who
seems to be the Millennium Falcon's co-pilot.

00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:46.630
She doesn't speak in the trailer, so the tone
of the droid is still unknown.

00:01:46.630 --> 00:01:50.100
She definitely seems to be one of the good
guys, and even has a nice little synchronized

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:53.370
salute with Lando, played by Donald Glover.

00:01:53.370 --> 00:01:54.480
New Falcon

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:57.890
How many times did you have to watch the trailer
before you realized this bright clean hallway

00:01:57.890 --> 00:02:00.050
belonged to the Millennium Falcon?

00:02:00.050 --> 00:02:04.920
By the time Luke comes on board the ship in
A New Hope, the place looks positively grimy.

00:02:04.920 --> 00:02:08.830
Fans knew Solo would show us how the smuggler
acquired the iconic vessel, but who knew it'd

00:02:08.830 --> 00:02:11.329
look like it was straight off the assembly
line?

00:02:11.329 --> 00:02:12.379
New baddies

00:02:12.379 --> 00:02:16.990
Han Solo goes literal space cowboy in his
first adventure, facing down a squad of bad-looking

00:02:16.990 --> 00:02:20.750
bandit dudes with nothing but his famous blaster
at his side.

00:02:20.750 --> 00:02:24.080
Exactly where this showdown is taking place
is still a very hidden detail, but he's certainly

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:25.880
not fighting the Empire here.

00:02:25.880 --> 00:02:29.990
This encounter is outlaw-on-outlaw, and it
looks like the same baddies take on Han on

00:02:29.990 --> 00:02:32.590
top of a train at one point in the film.

00:02:32.590 --> 00:02:34.010
New genre

00:02:34.010 --> 00:02:38.709
The new trailer also provides audiences their
first look at Thandie Newton playing a gun-toting,

00:02:38.709 --> 00:02:40.819
no-nonsense lady named Val.

00:02:40.819 --> 00:02:44.680
She's introduced in a brief clip while Woody
Harrelson's space pirate Tobias Beckett is

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:46.420
talking about getting a team together.

00:02:46.420 --> 00:02:50.260
Director Ron Howard has previously described
Solo as a heist movie, though we don't know

00:02:50.260 --> 00:02:52.299
yet what's being stolen and why.

00:02:52.299 --> 00:02:55.909
From the look of Newton's gigantic gun, her
character's probably what you'd call "the

00:02:55.909 --> 00:02:56.920
muscle."

00:02:56.920 --> 00:02:57.920
New critter

00:02:57.920 --> 00:03:02.080
The trailer also features a blink-and-you'll-miss-it
appearance by this little creature, a four-armed

00:03:02.080 --> 00:03:04.709
space monkey piloting some heavy machinery.

00:03:04.709 --> 00:03:08.409
It's hard to guess just how this alien critter
will figure into the story, but considering

00:03:08.409 --> 00:03:13.180
the dingy environment, it looks like he might
be messing around in the Spice Mines of Kessel,

00:03:13.180 --> 00:03:16.870
doing some dirty work with some sort of monkey-sized
machinery.

00:03:16.870 --> 00:03:17.969
New partner

00:03:17.969 --> 00:03:22.200
Here we see Emilia Clarke's mysterious Qi'ra
sitting side-by-side with Han travelling through

00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:26.209
what appears to be an Imperial base while
enemies follow in hot pursuit.

00:03:26.209 --> 00:03:30.430
In our first glimpse of Qi'ra in the teaser,
and in all her red-caped glory in the trailer,

00:03:30.430 --> 00:03:33.299
she appeared to be a straight-laced, stylish
figure of authority.

00:03:33.299 --> 00:03:36.639
But here she looks like an outlaw, the Bonnie
to Han's Clyde.

00:03:36.639 --> 00:03:39.279
Does he romance her out of an Imperial position
of authority?

00:03:39.279 --> 00:03:41.349
Or has she always been a scoundrel at heart?

00:03:41.349 --> 00:03:45.230
Either way, she's definitely on the run, but
she's got luck on her side — check out Han's

00:03:45.230 --> 00:03:47.390
gold dice hiding in plain sight.

00:03:47.390 --> 00:03:48.469
Thanks for watching!

00:03:48.469 --> 00:03:50.930
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:03:50.930 --> 00:03:52.659
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

